A lender's turn is charged after its borrower joins the run queue with a request on the lender's units,
which brought their virtual time up to the clock first, so the counts the turn ran before are charged on top,
and the borrower's request is over as it starts; a turn is charged at what it ran on, as it stood.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: a place waits on the run queue with no request open on its payer
Witness: fuzz-smp2 cores-lend-charges-first

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -928,7 +928,7 @@ void sched_lend(struct thread *t, struct notification *ntfn, struct thread *borr
      * The turn is charged first: the borrower may start a request on the units that pay for it,
      * which brings their virtual time up to the clock, and counts it ran before that are its to pay as they stood.
      */
-    uint64_t now = turn_close();
+    uint64_t now = timer_now();
     sched_wait(t, ntfn);
     lend_push(borrower, t);
